1
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:10,301
♪ Na na na na na
Na na na na na na na ♪

2
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:14,472
♪ I've gotta run run run to the store
Got it in spades and stacks on the floor ♪

3
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:17,267
♪ Spilling out the windows
Breaking down the doors ♪

4
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,645
♪ Y'all ready for more?
Do it do it like this ♪

5
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:24,274
[Jason] Let's have a team meeting.

6
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:28,194
First thing's first.
I don't know if you guys know,

7
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:30,739
me and Mary got into escrow on Doheny.
Nine point two million.

8
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,198
-[applause]
-[Mary] With the guy

9
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:33,908
I showed on my wedding day.

10
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:36,494
[Jason] And, by the way,
what an example of hard work.

11
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:39,164
Because that guy called me and said,
"I wanna see this house today."

12
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,166
I said, "No."
Then went around me and called her.

13
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:43,376
-I love that.
-She's like, "Yeah, I'll show you."

14
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,420
-She sold her own wedding venue…
-It's rewarding.

15
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:47,672
-…on her wedding day.
-[various] That's awesome.

16
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:50,383
I got into escrow with my client
for nine million yesterday.

17
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:53,803
Chrishell in escrow on Laurelwood,
4.1 million.

18
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,222
[Brett] That's the end
of a long road right there. Heather?

19
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:58,767
As of today,
I'm in escrow on Nichols Canyon.

20
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,268
-[Jason] There it is.
-[Mary] Yay!

21
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:03,188
[Heather] Despite the drama
at my broker's open. Thanks, ladies.

22
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,355
[laughter]

23
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,733
-It coulda been good luck. I don't know.
-[Jason] It wasn't.

24
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:08,193
[Brett, Mary] It's not.

25
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:09,611
I think it was good luck.

26
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:13,531
We're having our best week ever. We got
into over $20 million of escrow this week.

27
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:14,783
[Heather] That's awesome.

28
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,660
[Jason] And where is Amanza?
Has anybody talked to her?

29
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:23,458
She… the kids… don't have school today.
She's trying to get a last minute nanny.

30
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,210
-[Jason] Tired of the excuses.
-You asked!

31
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:28,004
-It's an excuse. That's why he's mad.
-Mary, a lot of people manage.

32
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:29,839
She's late
and says it'll never happen again.

33
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:32,300
-Tell her she can't be late.
-You're her boss, you tell her.

34
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:33,384
[Davina] You should.

35
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:36,054
I have. She says it'll never happen again.
I can show you the text.

36
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:38,848
-It happens for every single thing we do.
-I'm seriously--

37
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:40,517
If she's not gonna be reliable,

38
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,394
if I can't feel like
I can rely on her professionally

39
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:45,104
then she's gone.

40
00:01:46,731 --> 00:01:48,900
-Look who just showed up.
-[Amanza] Oh, hey!

41
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,903
-[Jason] Welcome.
-[all] Hi.

42
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:54,030
-[Heather] Uh-oh.
-[Maya] Right on time. [laughs]

43
00:01:54,405 --> 00:01:58,034
Listen, I have one flaw,
and that is that I am always late.

44
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:00,495
But… I show up.

45
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:03,581
-Davina, how about you?
-[Davina] Um, so…

46
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:06,251
So I still have Adnan's listing
for 75 million.

47
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:09,629
Obviously, the listing agreement
is close to expiring,

48
00:02:09,712 --> 00:02:11,297
so I've had a few showings.

49
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:12,882
I was talking to Christine.

50
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,593
Maybe we can work together
on bringing some people.

51
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:16,970
Maybe she has a database.

52
00:02:17,053 --> 00:02:19,180
You don't trust our database.
Only Christine's?

53
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:20,265
[Davina] No, I do.

54
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:22,767
[Maya] You don't know my database.
-[all laugh]

55
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,269
[Davina] That's true. That's true.

56
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:26,771
Christine's got some big whales
on her database, so…

57
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:28,690
[Jason] Alright. Christine?

58
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:31,943
Um, tonight is my broker's open,

59
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:36,906
doing burgers and Botox
to promote our newest listing.

60
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,992
[Jason] So you should pop by
and check it out.

61
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:39,909
Amanza?

62
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,911
-I'm just here for the coffee.
-[laughter]

63
00:02:42,453 --> 00:02:44,873
So I'm still looking
for someone to buy Stanley.

64
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:47,876
Doing my best,
open houses, broker's opens.

65
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:50,837
[Maya] You showing up on time
for the open houses?

66
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,797
I'm kidding, Amanza. I'm kidding.

67
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:58,178
No, I'm actually on time. I take snacks,
I take water, I show up, I look cute.

68
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:01,472
If you guys focused 100 percent on work
and put all the drama aside,

69
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:04,225
-you would all be unstoppable.
-[Amanza] Christine, are you listening?

70
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:05,768
Are you listening to this?

71
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:08,730
[Jason mumbles]

72
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:10,148
[various] Alright, go team.

73
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:12,817
Alright.
Well, I agree with Brett. Focus.

74
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:15,111
Amanza, let's have a conversation.

75
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:16,696
-[Jason] Thank you, guys.
-Alright.

76
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:18,531
-[Heather] You're in timeout.
-[Jason] Yeah.

77
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:21,242
[Christine] In school they made you sit
with your legs in a corner.

78
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:22,827
-[Jason] Alright.
-[laughter]

79
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:26,331
[Jason] Listen, you've been coming
in late. You're late for a lot of things.

80
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:28,124
It's really starting to frustrate me.

81
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:31,336
I don't have patience for that.
You've gotta understand.

82
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:34,088
I love you,
and you've got a ton of potential,

83
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:36,883
but being on time is super important.

84
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:39,928
I know. I'm sorry.
It's something I'm working on.

85
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:43,348
I've been working on it for a long time
with other stuff,

86
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:46,935
-and I've got a lot going on.
-[Jason] I know you have a lot going on,

87
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:49,145
but honestly you've had a timing issue
your whole life.

88
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:50,897
You have to focus on it.

89
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:53,608
-Yeah, I know.
-[Jason] Okay?

90
00:03:53,691 --> 00:03:54,901
Promise I'll work on it.

91
00:03:54,984 --> 00:03:55,818
Thanks.

92
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:59,697
♪ Then again ♪

93
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:04,077
♪ I'm feeling the rain come down ♪

94
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:08,414
♪ Rain on your head ♪

95
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:17,215
I'm really excited for this broker's open.
I'm doing a twilight event

96
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:19,259
and it's going to be burgers and Botox.

97
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:22,720
I would really want to create something
that everyone will remember,

98
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,764
and I mean, it is the two essentials:

99
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,933
food and Botox.

100
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:29,310
I mean, come on. I'm a genius. [scoffs]

101
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:34,816
[Christine] My co-listing agent, Monika,
wasn't on board with this event.

102
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:39,320
But I know this is exactly what we need
to create a buzz about this property.

103
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:40,488
["Werk" playing]

104
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:46,869
♪Oh oh oh oh we came to party
Oh oh oh oh let's get it started ♪

105
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:50,832
♪ And werk werk werk werk ♪

106
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:54,794
♪ Turn it up
Werk werk werk werk werk werk werk ♪

107
00:04:54,877 --> 00:04:58,715
♪ Turn it up
Werk werk werk werk… ♪

108
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:01,384
[Christine] Oh my God.
I really outdid myself.

109
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:02,552
[knocking]

110
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:04,846
-[Monika] Hi.
-Hi! How are you?

111
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:06,597
[Monika] Good. How are you?
Good seeing you.

112
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:09,350
-Good to see you. Hi.
-[Monika] You look lovely.

113
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,227
This is my sister, Ivy.

114
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:13,730
-Hi, so nice to meet you.
-She's been helping me

115
00:05:13,813 --> 00:05:15,106
with the open house--

116
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:17,567
-You look so much alike.
-Thanks. Beautiful color on you.

117
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,235
-Oh my gosh.
-Thank you. You look great.

118
00:05:19,318 --> 00:05:21,195
Do you have a lot of people coming?

119
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:22,947
-Yes.
-We do, yes.

120
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:25,366
Hopefully, they'll show up.
You know how LA is.

121
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:27,327
-You know?
-Yeah, I know.

122
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:30,830
-We have food, right?
-[Christine] So… I have some food.

123
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:34,000
I have the burgers here.
Botox lady's on the way.

124
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:36,085
-Obviously, this is a little more…
-Oh, wow. 

125
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,296
-… casual than I would've liked.
-We're doing the Botox?

126
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:41,299
I thought we could be more laid back,
not too-- not--

127
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:43,885
[Monika] Botox-- I think it's--

128
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:47,305
Um, we-- I wanted to do something
really, really big.

129
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:50,058
Like I said,
I thought it'd be more casual than this.

130
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:51,642
This is casual though, no?

131
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:53,686
This is casual. Burgers are casual.

132
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,897
And I invited every broker in Los Angeles.

133
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:58,733
So I feel like if we do Botox,
they're gonna come.

134
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:01,611
We're in Hollywood after all, right?

135
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:03,988
Then we have some wine
and, you know, drinks.

136
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:06,449
We could booze people up
before we put needles in them.

137
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:12,747
It's definitely not
your regular broker's open--

138
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:14,415
-[Christine] I know. [giggles]
-… right?

139
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:18,336
[Christine] Hi, guys!

140
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:20,630
What a fun concept! Burgers and Botox.

141
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,800
[Amanza] Wait. Quinn-N-Out?
Like your last name. That's super cute.

142
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:25,093
I know.

143
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:29,055
So Jason has been adamant
that I step it up at work.

144
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:34,143
It's just annoying that my first chance
to do that is at an event for Christine.

145
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:37,021
However,
there's burgers and there's Botox.

146
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:39,482
Two things that I really love,

147
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:42,652
so that's gonna get me there.

148
00:06:42,735 --> 00:06:45,988
-[Brett] It looks great. Good to see you.
-[Christine] Look at you in your jackets!

149
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:49,033
-[Amanza] You gonna get some Botox?
-I got Botox yesterday, so you won't know

150
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,701
-if I like the house.
-[Christine] Really?

151
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:53,663
-[Jason] No. This looks cute, by the way.
-This is insane.

152
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:54,664
[all] Hi!

153
00:06:54,747 --> 00:06:57,625
Wow. In-N-- Wait, from where?

154
00:06:57,708 --> 00:07:02,505
"Quinn-N-Out," look. That is so cute.
Is that one vegan?

155
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,967
-[Mary] Is it Botox anytime or… ?
-I don't now, let's see.

156
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,385
Let's find out the deal.

157
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:12,140
-Basically, my whole face.
-[nurse] I'm gonna take some make-up off.

158
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:14,892
Guys, I'm so excited.
We're here at my broker's open

159
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,936
and it is burgers and Botox.

160
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:22,483
I'm not gonna lie, I'm pushing 40,
like, any month now,

161
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:26,821
and if a little Botox can help me
look like myself…

162
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:29,490
shoot me up.

163
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,118
So feel free to get some Botox.

164
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:34,370
In the meantime,
I wanna show you guys around the house.

165
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,621
So this is super gorgeous.

166
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:39,917
This is 4,100 square feet,
views of the city.

167
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,669
[Amanza] Oh my gosh.

168
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:44,213
Upstairs has a golf course.

169
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:46,924
-[Jason] Let's go golfing.
-[Maya] I wanna see the upstairs.

170
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,467
[Brett] Let's put money on this.

171
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:50,469
-Hundred bucks I get closer.
-[Jason] I'll bet.

172
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:53,139
[Maya] If I try to golf,
I'll probably smash someone's window.

173
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:54,307
[Davina] Don't do it.

174
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:58,186
[Brett] Oh my God,
that's the putt of my life.

175
00:07:58,269 --> 00:08:00,188
[Maya] You always fighting
for the same holes.

176
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:02,273
-[Davina] Gross!
-[Jason] Shut up, Maya.

177
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:03,357
[laughter]

178
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:05,902
[Maya] That's why they have to be quiet.
Have to focus.

179
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:08,112
[Maya giggles] Boo!

180
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:10,323
[Heather] Oh, not hard enough.

181
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:13,784
-[Jason] I've never heard that.
-Been nice doing business with you.

182
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:14,869
Good putt, bro.

183
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:17,496
-Huh?
-[Maya] That was aggressive. 

184
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:19,874
[Maya] Nice pose, Heather.

185
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:23,753
[Brett] Where are you aiming? Hold on.
You're aiming over there. You're going--

186
00:08:23,836 --> 00:08:26,797
-[Heather] I'm not ready yet!
-[Jason] Can I see a practice swing first?

187
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:29,717
Just to see if you're gonna--
Don't go nearly that hard.

188
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,718
[Heather screams] What?

189
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:31,719
[Davina] Go, Heather.

190
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:33,888
[Heather] You do your thing, I do mine.
Watch out.

191
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,139
[Amanza] Heather, go!

192
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:38,434
-This will be the worst putt of all time.
-[Davina] Can you hit the ball?

193
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:39,769
-You guys!
-[Davina] Go!

194
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,686
[Heather] Ready?

195
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:41,812
[Maya] Uh-oh.

196
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:44,982
-[Jason] Yes, Jesus. Oh, man.
-[Amanza] Way off.

197
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:47,777
-[Maya] Through the neighbor's house.
-[Heather] That was good.

198
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,988
-Hi, guys. Christine.
-Hey, Christine. Asaf.

199
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,698
Asaf, nice to meet you.

200
00:08:52,823 --> 00:08:53,991
-This is gorgeous.
-Hi.

201
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:57,703
You wanna get people to come
to your broker's open in LA? [clicks]

202
00:08:57,787 --> 00:08:59,872
-Botox.
-[Jason] Veggie burgers and Botox.

203
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:01,749
Heather's like, "Yeah, I'm there."

204
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:03,292
Four bedroom, five bathroom.

205
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:05,753
-There's a lot of people here.
-I know it looks great.

206
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:08,005
[Christine singing] So excited.

207
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:10,841
You should do some.
-[Jason] You should do some more.

208
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:12,134
[Christine laughs]

209
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:15,555
Christine, I've seen burgers,
but I've never seen Botox.

210
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:18,432
It's fun though.
People are coming. It's working.

211
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:21,102
-Good job. It's a good show out.
-[Christine] I'm happy you came!

212
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:23,312
-[Jason] Good job.
-[Christine] This was so fun.

213
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:27,275
♪ All around the world
They want, they gotta have it ♪

214
00:09:27,358 --> 00:09:30,987
♪ Everywhere I go
Feeling fabulous ♪

215
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:34,407
♪ Mm-mm-mm… ♪

216
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,914
You tired, Brett?
Did you wake up before noon today?

217
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:43,165
Eight-thirty.

218
00:09:43,874 --> 00:09:45,126
[scoffs]

219
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:48,212
I love those shoes. I wouldn't wear them
'cause I cannot pull that off,

220
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,797
but you can totally pull it off.

221
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,632
Might be the best outfit
anyone's ever worn.

222
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:53,759
I just threw this together. I wasn't sure.

223
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:56,971
[Chrishell] You really gotta work on
figuring out how to express yourself.

224
00:09:57,054 --> 00:10:00,016
[Jasons laughs] You gotta come out
of your shell, Christine.

225
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,476
[Christine laughs] I know.

226
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:03,978
[slurps loudly]

227
00:10:04,061 --> 00:10:06,022
-[Jason] Anyone hungry?
-Yes.

228
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:08,024
-I'm starving.
-[Chrishell] Question…

229
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:12,028
When you're really hungry
and you eat a smoothie, have a smoothie,

230
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:14,780
how long until you have to eat again?
Because it can't last that long.

231
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:18,367
Here's the thing, I don't get hungry.
Ever. I get low blood sugar

232
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:22,121
and I'm low blood pressure
and low blood sugar. I'll get dizzy.

233
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:25,291
-[Heather] But smoothies fill me up a lot.
-Yeah.

234
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,752
Hey, I have something for you.

235
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:32,757
[Jason] It's just 1.6,
but it's a lot of activity.

236
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:36,427
-I think it's dope.
-[Jason] An easy double-end, I think.

237
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:38,179
[Mary] That is a dope house.

238
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:41,307
So is Jason giving Mary another listing?

239
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:42,850
-I'm sure.
-What about us?

240
00:10:43,934 --> 00:10:45,936
I need to call for sale by owner
to get something.

241
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:49,148
-I need to go door-knock. [laughs]
-Oh God.

242
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,569
[Christine] Favoritism at its best.

243
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,531
-[dog barks]
-[Jason] Come here, baby girl.

244
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:00,868
-[Amanza] Hi.
-Hey.

245
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,995
I'm coming to your desk,
but not in trouble this time.

246
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:03,913
Okay.

247
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:07,458
I have a question for you…
about my Stanley listing.

248
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:13,339
I have this… person
who's not ready to buy just quite yet,

249
00:11:13,881 --> 00:11:16,133
but he would be interested in leasing.

250
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:17,885
So why isn't the house selling?

251
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:20,846
I don't know.

252
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:23,724
[Amanza] I mean, I looked at comps
with Mary just the other day.

253
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:27,937
It's listed right around
a thousand square foot. Um…

254
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:31,232
I don't know.
It seems like it's listed perfectly.

255
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,110
I know it's not, like, ideal,

256
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:37,655
but if I haven't gotten any, you know,
firm offers from anyone else.

257
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:40,574
Do you think that's something
that would be appropriate,

258
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,411
to present a lease
rather than come to him with a buyer?

259
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:45,079
[Jason] The answer is this:

260
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:47,081
you have to present everything
to your client.

261
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:49,834
Anytime you get an offer,
whether it's lease, sell,

262
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:52,002
it's your obligation to go to your client

263
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:54,630
and give him that information
and let him make a decision.

264
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:58,676
If you don't think you can sell it…
leasing's better than nothing.

265
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:00,886
-Yeah. Okay.
-Barely. Yeah, barely.

266
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:02,138
That sucks.

267
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:06,183
Make sure your tenant's a real tenant.
He's not throwing in some shitty offer.

268
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:08,394
So what do you think
a fair lease price is?

269
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:11,856
What's the asking price on Stanley,
2.4 million?

270
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:15,109
You usually get
about 4,000 dollars per million,

271
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:16,444
on just a rule of thumb.

272
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:20,114
So a reasonable lease
is around 11,000 dollars a month.

273
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,782
-Yeah.
-I think the bottom line is,

274
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,701
you need to go to your client and say,

275
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:26,537
"Listen, you've got a lease opportunity.
Are you interested?"

276
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:27,455
Okay.

277
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:30,499
-Talk to him and let me know what he says.
-Alright. Thank you.

278
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:33,002
[Mary] Don't worry. You got this.

279
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:37,506
It sucks because I'm trying to navigate
my way through this real estate thing,

280
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,925
and I just feel like
a huge disappointment.

281
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:43,554
You know, my first offer's a lease
and the boys are just, like…

282
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:45,473
not having it.

283
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:47,892
I am starving. Let's go eat.

284
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:52,313
-Oh, I am too, actually.
-I need to make this phone call.

285
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,023
-Yeah.
-[Mary] Okay.

286
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,193
I'm really hard on myself.
Like, everything is my fault.

287
00:12:57,276 --> 00:13:01,405
It makes it ten times harder
when I don't achieve right away.

288
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:03,908
I'm scared
and don't always know what I'm doing.

289
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:07,286
I have so many questions,
and I'm scared to even ask the questions

290
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:10,164
because these are my closest friends.
So…

291
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:13,959
you know, it's hard to be vulnerable
around people that you've always been,

292
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:15,085
like, the tough one.

293
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:23,886
[Amanza] You think I'm doing a good job,
right, Zelda?

294
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:30,935
♪ Solid gold vibe eh
Solid gold vibe ♪

295
00:13:31,393 --> 00:13:34,146
♪ Where'd she get that bag?
Where'd she get that swag? ♪

296
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,774
♪ Oh that body bag
Really want me one like that ♪

297
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:39,819
♪ I'm like a Barbie in real life
Yeah I keep it real tight ♪

298
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:42,905
♪Snuck up in your mind
With my solid gold vibe eh! ♪

299
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,617
-[Christine] Hi, how are you?
-Good to see you.

300
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:47,660
Hi, good to see you too.

301
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,620
-This is Christine and Shena.
-Hi, how are you?

302
00:13:49,703 --> 00:13:51,747
-Christine, nice to meet you.
-Come on in.

303
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:55,334
Mr. Adnan,
Davina and Christine are here to see you.

304
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:56,961
-Great.
-[Davina] Hi.

305
00:13:57,044 --> 00:14:00,256
I haven't had any offers
on my 75 million dollar listing.

306
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:04,051
After seeing how creative and successful
Christine's broker open was

307
00:14:04,134 --> 00:14:05,511
with the burgers and Botox,

308
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:08,305
I'm really hoping she can channel
some of that towards my listing.

309
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:12,059
If anyone knows how a millionaire
wants to live, it's Christine.

310
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:15,813
So what do you think
you can bring to the table?

311
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,690
It's all about clients and who you know.

312
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:21,193
I have an extensive database
that I could hopefully round up--

313
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,945
-[Davina] Tap into. Yeah.
-…and tap into

314
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:25,823
and see if I can find someone
that might be right for this house.

315
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:27,449
I'm not promising anything,

316
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:31,412
but I do know that this house is amazing.
I've loved it from day one.

317
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:34,748
And I feel like
I might be able to help facilitate

318
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:37,084
at least some interest on this house.

319
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:41,755
It has been so long and I have not seen
anything concrete on the table yet.

320
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,008
-[Davina] That's why we're here.
-You guys… 

321
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,760
everyday, not selling,
it's costing me a fortune.

322
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:50,764
[Adnan] For me,
the most important thing is the result.

323
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:53,601
I mean, it took us three and a half years
to build here.

324
00:14:53,684 --> 00:14:56,562
Wow. What did you buy the property for
when you bought it?

325
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:01,358
We should be discussing
how you can sell it,

326
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:04,612
-as I also told her in the beginning--
-In addition to that, I'd love to know--

327
00:15:04,695 --> 00:15:07,531
You should not negotiate with me,
you should negotiate with the customers.

328
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:09,867
-This is what I always say--
-It's not a negotiation to ask

329
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:13,037
about the lot that you would love me
to help be a part of.

330
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:18,542
[Christine] It's off of Coldwater Canyon,
there's no view and it's a very busy road.

331
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:22,671
I'm trying to justify a price
so that when I bring people in here,

332
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,466
I can tell them
that this is the most amazing property,

333
00:15:25,549 --> 00:15:29,011
and every cent that I'm trying to sell
is justified.

334
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:32,598
♪ Not holding back anymore ♪

335
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:51,867
[Chrishell] Jason, did you see this?
For Coldwater?

336
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:55,496
I did not.

337
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:58,207
Ah! You gotta check it out.

338
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:00,668
This is one of the photos
you're talking about.

339
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,921
-But look at the two-- two pages!
-[Jason] That looks good.

340
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:06,173
-[Jason] You wrote the description?
-[Chrishell] I did.

341
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:08,175
I'm gonna look for grammar.
Hold on, gimme a sec.

342
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:10,594
[Davina] Oh my God. Only Jason would.

343
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:12,096
I had Angelica look over it.

344
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:14,014
[Jason] No, it looks really good.
Good job.

345
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:16,266
And with that…

346
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:19,144
-[Chrishell] That was dramatic.
-I'm out.

347
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:21,313
-You're out of here?
-[Jason] Good job, again.

348
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:23,107
-Thank you.
-[Jason] See ya.

349
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,024
Have a good day.

350
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:26,068
[Jason] You're outlasting me today,
good job.

351
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,236
-Yeah.
-Right?

352
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:28,487
[Davina sighs]

353
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:32,449
Okay. Now that he's gone,
we don't have to work.

354
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,368
[Davina laughs] Yeah, it's true.

355
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:37,121
That was actually really fun
for Christine's birthday.

356
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:39,289
-Like, the tarot card--
-Good. I'm glad you had fun.

357
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,500
-The restaurant was so cute. I love that.
-Right?

358
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:43,752
They did a good job
with the cocktails and stuff.

359
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:46,505
I did think we might get kicked out
at one point, but…

360
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:49,800
I was caught off guard with Amanza.
She's coming out of left field,

361
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:52,428
attacking Christine. I was like,
what is happening right now?

362
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:53,679
I was so uncomfortable.

363
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:56,140
How does she even know
what Christine said,

364
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:58,767
and why would she say it at her birthday?
I was like, "Oh my God."

365
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,310
I told Amanza and Mary.

366
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:02,896
-Why would you tell her?
-Everyone knew about it.

367
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:05,899
You think it was gonna be a thing
where Amanza wasn't gonna find out?

368
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:09,278
But Amanza's, like,
such a bully bodyguard with--

369
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:13,115
you know, for Mary. It should've stayed
between Mary and Christine.

370
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:15,409
Heather didn't get involved.
And, you know…

371
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,578
I don't know, I didn't get involved.

372
00:17:18,078 --> 00:17:20,372
Amanza and Mary and I are all very close.

373
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:23,083
There's no scenario
in which I tell Mary something

374
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:26,795
and Amanza doesn't find out anyway.
Christine's actions, like, was rude.

375
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:29,423
It's not okay to do what she did
at a broker's open--

376
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:34,094
Let me finish. Not okay to do what she did
at a broker's open in front of clients.

377
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:38,307
I don't like what she said,
but it's coming from a place of hurt

378
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,517
that her and Mary
kinda drifted apart more.

379
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:43,604
Yeah, and hurt people hurt people,
and that's what Christine does,

380
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:46,607
and I don't think that's a reason
to defend bad behavior.

381
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:47,691
But…

382
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:50,110
Yeah. No, but--

383
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:54,948
The days of Christine, like, being, like,
this tyrannical type of, like,

384
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:57,993
"Only people can do and say
what I approve,"

385
00:17:58,077 --> 00:18:00,079
and stuff like that
in this office are over--

386
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:02,039
I think she's going to be who she is.

387
00:18:02,122 --> 00:18:03,707
You know what I mean? So--

388
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:07,419
-Yeah. Sometimes that's a problem.
-You didn't have to involve Amanza.

389
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:09,463
[Davina] You didn't have to.

390
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:12,883
Christine involved
the whole office and clients.

391
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:17,805
I'm gonna have to leave it at that,
'cause honestly, it's, like, lunacy to me

392
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:19,765
that you care that I told Amanza,

393
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:25,312
but you don't care that Christine told
the whole West Side at a broker's--

394
00:18:25,395 --> 00:18:28,482
I just think you're adding fuel
to the fire that wasn't necessary.

395
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:30,526
That's all I'm saying. It was too much.

396
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:34,446
-All of us were uncomfortable.
-Oh my God. Okay. I'm getting a headache.

397
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,365
-Why add?
-Oh my God, Davina!

398
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:41,245
Look… I'm going to defend my friends,
and I know you're defending your friend.

399
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:43,956
I don't really see how you can defend
what Christine did.

400
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:46,250
I can't be held responsible
for what she said.

401
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:49,002
-Okay.
-Right, but what you did was your choice.

402
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:52,422
And I would choose that again every single
time because those are my friends.

403
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,550
-So agree to disagree.
-Okay.

404
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:56,009
-Okay.
-Sounds good to me.

405
00:18:56,426 --> 00:18:57,302
[Chrishell sighs]

406
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:09,565
♪ I hear the beat so ready to
Burn this down, burn this down ♪

407
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:12,818
-It's so hot. Are you hot?
-[Noah laughs]

408
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:16,238
-[Noah] Yeah. I'm going on the red thing.
-[Amanza] Okay. What's the red thing?

409
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:18,365
-[Noah] Climb it, Mommy.
-[Amanza] Can I? I can,

410
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:21,034
but might break something.
We can make an obstacle course.

411
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,786
-Yeah.
-[Amanza] I could time.

412
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,663
We can see who does it the fastest, okay?

413
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:27,833
This new schedule with real estate,
it's so grueling, 

414
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:30,335
that I've been missing
so much time with my kids.

415
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:36,300
It's hard because I'm torn, you know.
I made the right decision to work longer

416
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:40,304
and more on this real estate thing.
I have mom guilt, like, extreme mom guilt.

417
00:19:40,387 --> 00:19:43,307
So I'm just excited to connect with them

418
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:46,810
and, you know,
get a little mommy time with the kiddos.

419
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:49,104
[Amanza] Braker, ready, go!

420
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:54,693
[laughs] Oh look, he's moving so--
Your shoe's untied. Please be careful.

421
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:56,570
[Noah laughs]

422
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:59,656
[Amanza] Go down! Watch your shoelace!
Push-up! Whoop whoop!

423
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,700
-That was a jumping push-up.
-Stop!

424
00:20:01,783 --> 00:20:03,994
-[Noah] That was 16.02.
-16.27.

425
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:06,747
Woo! Okay, ready?

426
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,707
-[Noah] Set. Go.
-[Braker] Fifty seconds.

427
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:12,711
[Amanza screams] You said 50 seconds,
Braker? How rude! [laughs]

428
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:15,422
Oh, I think I'm gonna win this time!

429
00:20:15,505 --> 00:20:17,507
Oh my God. I almost broke my neck.

430
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:24,473
-[Braker] 21.
-21.40

431
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:27,142
-[Braker laughs]
-Okay. Clearly, I won.

432
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:29,478
-[Noah] No, Braker won.
-What?

433
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:31,730
-[kids] Yeah.
-No, I smoked Braker.

434
00:20:31,813 --> 00:20:34,107
Don't I get, like, a pass, like a…

435
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:35,400
An old pass.

436
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:38,737
-Yeah, an old lady pass.
-[Noah] You don't get an old lady pass.

437
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:42,199
Are you gonna sit with us or are you just
gonna sit over there by yourself?

438
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:44,785
-[Noah] I'll sit.
-I think I should get an old lady pass.

439
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,203
-No!
-Why?

440
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:47,162
One point.

441
00:20:47,245 --> 00:20:51,208
You know when you go to a restaurant,
if you're 65 or older you get a discount?

442
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:52,584
Seriously? [giggles]

443
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:55,420
What do you think, now that mommy
started selling real estate?

444
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:58,131
Today was the first day that I picked you
up from school for a while.

445
00:20:58,215 --> 00:20:59,091
[Noah] Mm-hmm.

446
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:01,260
-And you're not quite used to that. Huh?
-No.

447
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:04,554
I think I'm better at decorating houses,

448
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,848
not quite at selling houses yet.

449
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:09,309
-That's a lot harder.
-You got one!

450
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:11,186
Well, I have one listing.

451
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:14,690
-Oh.
-But I don't-- I haven't sold it yet.

452
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:18,902
Well, we believe in you, and we know
you can sell a house and a building.

453
00:21:18,986 --> 00:21:19,861
You do?

454
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:21,029
[Braker] Mm-hmm.

455
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:24,074
You are so sweet. Thank you.
So, what do you guys think?

456
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:28,954
Do you think
that mommy made a better home-stager,

457
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:31,915
designer, or real estate agent?

458
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:34,334
I kinda like that you're in real estate

459
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:36,253
'cause you can make more money
for yourself.

460
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:40,757
Oh! Look at you, Mr. Business.
Braker's right, you do make more money.

461
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:43,385
It's just, it's a lot harder
than I thought it was gonna be.

462
00:21:43,468 --> 00:21:44,970
[Noah] You're doing really good.

463
00:21:45,053 --> 00:21:47,973
You can make more money for,
like, how daddy left off.

464
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,767
So you can make more money for that,

465
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:54,104
to buy more groceries
and, like, whatever you want.

466
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,570
-I'm proud of you.
-[Amanza] You're proud of me?

467
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:03,780
-[Noah] I'm proud of you too.
-You guys are sweet.

468
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:06,325
-Who made you so sweet?
-[Braker] Mommy, are you crying?

469
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:09,036
-[Noah] I don't want to see you cry.
-[kisses] I love you.

470
00:22:10,704 --> 00:22:12,289
[Noah] I know that you can do it.

471
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:17,127
Can I get a kiss? I love you.

472
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:20,005
[Braker] I love you too.
I'll always be by your side.

473
00:22:20,088 --> 00:22:21,840
You will? Always?

474
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:24,843
It motivates me to work harder
after hearing them say

475
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:27,429
that they're proud of me. But it also…

476
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:30,974
A bit of a breath of fresh air
to know they're not angry with you.

477
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:33,727
They're not--
You know, there's no resentment

478
00:22:33,810 --> 00:22:36,188
and they're really cheering me on.

479
00:22:37,064 --> 00:22:39,149
They're so sweet and they…

480
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,611
they see how hard I'm working…

481
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:45,113
and instead of…
He could have easily been, like,

482
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:48,408
"No, I want to spend more time
with my mommy." They really get it

483
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:52,120
and they understand
what's happening and um…

484
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:54,289
I don't know.

485
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:57,959
It shook me, but they're just--
They're freaking awesome.

486
00:22:58,043 --> 00:23:00,629
And that just makes me want to go out

487
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:03,340
and just work even harder
and make them more proud.

488
00:23:03,924 --> 00:23:08,220
I hope you sell the listing
and then you can buy me a trampoline.

489
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:10,430
-[all laugh]
-[Amanza] Of course.

490
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:14,101
-I promise you, if I sell it.
-Okay. [laughs]

491
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:15,852
I'll buy you a trampoline.
-Okay.

492
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:18,980
♪ I love my money
And my money loves me… ♪

493
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:26,488
[Christine laughs]

494
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:29,741
♪ I don't really care
Imma be a billionaire… ♪

495
00:23:33,703 --> 00:23:35,580
-Isn't it gorgeous?
-[Christian] Yeah.

496
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:39,584
I'm bringing Christian to Davina's listing
because he is a baller.

497
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:42,921
He worked as a tech entrepreneur,
and he knows tons of people

498
00:23:43,004 --> 00:23:45,340
in Silicon Valley that might be
great clients for this house.

499
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:47,175
-What's the price?
-[Christine] Seventy-five.

500
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:50,804
The main house has seven bedrooms
and ten bathrooms. So it's huge.

501
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:54,558
I know Christian well enough to know
that he's not gonna bring his friends

502
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:58,103
or a potential client to this house
if he can't run the numbers

503
00:23:58,186 --> 00:24:00,689
and see where the price is coming from.

504
00:24:00,772 --> 00:24:03,525
Between my real estate expertise
and Christian's connections,

505
00:24:03,608 --> 00:24:06,486
if we can't sell this house,
I don't know who can.

506
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:07,946
Take a look and see if you have

507
00:24:08,029 --> 00:24:10,157
-anyone in mind for this property.
-Yeah.

508
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:12,367
-That's the whole reason we're here.
-Okay.

509
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:15,078
[Christian] Wondering about the price
because 18,000 square feet--

510
00:24:15,162 --> 00:24:17,122
[Christine] Little more
than 4,000 a square foot.

511
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:19,040
[Christian] Is that a guest house?

512
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:22,627
[Christine] There's a guest house
totaling 3,000 square feet.

513
00:24:22,711 --> 00:24:24,880
And an additional two bedrooms out there.

514
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,298
This is the master suite.

515
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:29,092
His-and-hers closet.

516
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:30,760
I like how it's split up.

517
00:24:30,844 --> 00:24:33,513
-With a gym. I love the gym.
-[Christian] And there's a gym. Great.

518
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:36,933
-[Both] A little plunge pool.
-[Christine] Isn't it gorgeous?

519
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:41,104
[Christian] So the bedrooms are basically
upstairs with the guest bedroom here.

520
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:42,981
[Christian] You said this was on an acre?

521
00:24:43,064 --> 00:24:46,151
[Christine] Yeah. This is an acre lot.
They bought this in 2013.

522
00:24:46,234 --> 00:24:48,778
-And all these open up all the way.
-[Christian] Mm-hmm.

523
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:52,157
-Um, this is a beautiful house.
-I got it. I'm the real estate agent.

524
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,450
-You're doing it?
-Thank you.

525
00:24:53,533 --> 00:24:55,577
-Still, I would be the one doing it--
-So rude.

526
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:56,786
Looks like you're struggling.

527
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:59,206
-This is-- No, I'm the real estate agent.
-Okay. [laughs]

528
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:00,999
This is why I get paid
the mediocre dollars.

529
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,418
Just to struggle with heavy things?

530
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,379
-[Christine] So what do you think?
-[Christian] Okay.

531
00:25:06,838 --> 00:25:10,217
[Christian] Uh, It's obviously
a spectacular house, let me say that.

532
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:11,760
I don't understand the asking price.

533
00:25:11,843 --> 00:25:14,137
I'm still trying to get to
the 4,000 a square foot number,

534
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:16,598
and if you want me to ask my friends
to come see it,

535
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:19,059
I have to make sense out of the economics.

536
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:23,813
[Christine] Let's look at the rest
of the house because it's fantastic.

537
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:25,732
Maybe it'll help justify
the price for you.

538
00:25:25,815 --> 00:25:26,650
Okay.

539
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:28,944
I'm putting an effort to help Davina,

540
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:32,113
even though I know it's overpriced,
because she is a friend of mine.

541
00:25:32,197 --> 00:25:34,991
And obviously, I wanna make
a million dollar commission. Who wouldn't?

542
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:37,744
So it's kind of a win-win situation.

543
00:25:37,827 --> 00:25:40,705
But first I have to get to the bottom
of the price.

544
00:25:42,123 --> 00:25:44,501
[Christine] Hi. How are you?

545
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:46,419
This is my fiancé, Christian.

546
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:49,673
-So nice to finally meet you.
-Hi, Christian. Nice to meet you.

547
00:25:49,756 --> 00:25:50,715
[Christine] Good timing.

548
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:52,717
[Adnan] Yeah. You're gonna go
around the house?

549
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:54,761
[Christian] We took a look.
It's beautiful.

550
00:25:54,844 --> 00:25:57,847
I had to understand the math of it,
but I love the house, obviously.

551
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:59,933
-Spectacular house.
-[Christine] Gorgeous.

552
00:26:00,642 --> 00:26:02,352
Yes, it is an expensive project,

553
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:07,315
but very rare to have two lots,
especially in Beverly Hills, you know.

554
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:09,192
What did you buy the lots for?

555
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:14,364
[Adnan] What we are building
is top-of-the-line.

556
00:26:14,447 --> 00:26:17,033
If you want a really good thing,
the client has to pay for it.

557
00:26:18,410 --> 00:26:21,955
Not being able to get information
and answers out of Adnan, it's…

558
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:24,916
making it hard to justify the price.

559
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:29,379
All I hear is "Grade A. Top quality.
Grade A."

560
00:26:29,796 --> 00:26:30,880
Good stuff costs.

561
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:34,592
Took us over three and a half years
to build.

562
00:26:34,676 --> 00:26:37,387
-Four years. Exactly. Oh, yeah.
-[Christine] Wow.

563
00:26:37,470 --> 00:26:40,265
It is a pain. I mean, it is, but…

564
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:43,143
-someone has to do the job, right?
-[Christian] Mm-hmm.

565
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:45,437
Well, I love it. I think it's fantastic

566
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:49,107
and I hope we can find a buyer
that'll love this house for you guys.

567
00:26:49,190 --> 00:26:53,445
So far, I see you guys are doing great
effort, but it's all about the result.

568
00:26:53,528 --> 00:26:57,073
We'll have updates soon, and it was great
to see you guys. Bye, babies!

569
00:26:57,157 --> 00:26:59,075
Let's be in contact. Say hi to Davina.

570
00:26:59,159 --> 00:27:00,493
-I will, definitely.
-Alright.

571
00:27:01,494 --> 00:27:02,912
[Adnan] You're not going. Come.

572
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:06,416
-[Christian] What are the property taxes?
-[Christine] A lot.

573
00:27:13,506 --> 00:27:16,259
♪ Watch me do it like this ♪

574
00:27:18,345 --> 00:27:20,138
♪ Like this… ♪

575
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:25,393
Hello.

576
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:27,103
-Hey!
-[Preston] How's it going?

577
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:29,564
-How are you? Good to see you.
-[Preston] Good. You too.

578
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:30,815
[Mary] Congrats.

579
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:31,816
You too.

580
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,902
-Congrats, man.
-[Preston] Thank you. You too.

581
00:27:33,985 --> 00:27:37,405
-Thank you again so much for showing.
-[repeating] Oh, my pleasure.

582
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,782
[Mary] How's your client feeling?

583
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,450
-Super excited?
-[Preston] Very excited.

584
00:27:40,533 --> 00:27:41,993
We've done a few together. I love it.

585
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:44,663
-It's awesome, let's keep going.
-[Jason] What's that saying?

586
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:47,207
Ten percent of the agents
do 90 percent of the business.

587
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:50,794
-[both men] It's 100 percent true.
-[Jason] Mary, want to do the honors?

588
00:27:50,877 --> 00:27:53,213
-[Mary] There you go. Congratulations.
-[Preston] Awesome.

589
00:27:53,296 --> 00:27:54,756
Thanks. Every key should come like this.

590
00:27:54,839 --> 00:27:56,591
-[Jason] I know, right.
-[Mary] I know.

591
00:27:56,675 --> 00:27:59,302
-It was awesome working with you.
-[Preston] Thanks. Such a pleasure.

592
00:27:59,386 --> 00:28:01,304
[Jason] Good job. You're always great.

593
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:02,806
-See you later.
-Bye.

594
00:28:02,889 --> 00:28:03,723
Ciao, bud.

595
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:08,019
-Yay Zelda, we did it!
-[Jason] Dude, did I--? Good job, babe.

596
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:11,815
I think I'm probably the first agent

597
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:14,359
to sell my wedding venue
on my wedding day.

598
00:28:14,442 --> 00:28:16,361
[cheering, applause]

599
00:28:16,444 --> 00:28:19,739
I feel like a badass right now.
I'm so proud of myself

600
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:23,576
and I never thought I would be here.
Since I had my son at such a young age,

601
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,954
and I mean, working these brutal jobs

602
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:28,957
just to barely, barely get by.

603
00:28:29,457 --> 00:28:32,377
And now I just appreciate
the value of a dollar,

604
00:28:32,460 --> 00:28:37,257
and I want to make sure
I always have a lot of them in my account.

605
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:41,219
How does it feel to be rich
after selling your wedding venue?

606
00:28:41,302 --> 00:28:44,764
-[laughs] No more money twitch.
-Now it's gonna be a money dance.

607
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:45,724
Oh yeah.

608
00:28:46,391 --> 00:28:48,726
It went from this… to this.

609
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:51,479
But my dancing skills are meh…
not so great.

610
00:28:54,107 --> 00:28:55,024
This is Amanza.

611
00:28:56,109 --> 00:28:58,236
[phone] Hi, Amanza, it's Lisa.
How are you?

612
00:28:58,319 --> 00:29:00,113
Hi, Lisa, I'm well. How are you?

613
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:04,492
I'm good.
I am calling with not such great news.

614
00:29:05,076 --> 00:29:08,955
Unfortunately, my client that wanted
to lease the Stanley property

615
00:29:09,038 --> 00:29:12,292
is not interested anymore
because they want--

616
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:14,544
They're looking
for a work-at-home type of situation.

617
00:29:14,627 --> 00:29:17,046
They're concerned
that there'd be issues with the neighbors.

618
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:19,215
So now they're just gonna look
for an office space.

619
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:21,926
Kind of a bummer for both of us,
I'm sorry.

620
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:24,763
It is a bit of a bummer,
but if you have other buyers

621
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:26,473
that potentially want to see it,

622
00:29:26,556 --> 00:29:29,392
I'm happy to show them
because it will still be for sale.

623
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:34,272
And maybe, you know, we could just find
somebody to buy it instead. [chuckles]

624
00:29:34,355 --> 00:29:36,941
Yeah, absolutely.
I'm gonna let my colleague know as well,

625
00:29:37,025 --> 00:29:40,236
because this is a great property.
And we'll be in touch soon. Hopefully.

626
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:42,530
Okay, I appreciate the phone call.
Thank you.

627
00:29:42,947 --> 00:29:45,575
-You're welcome, talk to you soon. Bye.
-Okay, bye.

628
00:29:48,077 --> 00:29:50,872
-Well, that kind of sucked.
-[Mary] They're not gonna lease it now?

629
00:29:50,955 --> 00:29:54,209
They want to work from home,
and they're afraid it'll be too loud.

630
00:29:54,292 --> 00:29:55,960
Yeah. So does he know?

631
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:57,879
[Amanza groans]

632
00:29:58,713 --> 00:30:02,509
I feel like I'm failing everybody,
and I'm trying to prove myself

633
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:03,551
to so many people.

634
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:07,096
I'm trying to prove myself to Jason
for giving me the opportunity

635
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:09,891
to be an agent at his brokerage.

636
00:30:09,974 --> 00:30:13,645
Trying to prove myself to my kids
that I can take care of them

637
00:30:13,728 --> 00:30:16,898
and keep a roof over their head
and feed them.

638
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:21,194
But, like, this is the most successful
real estate agency in West Hollywood.

639
00:30:21,277 --> 00:30:24,364
And I'm, you know,
sitting at a desk here every day,

640
00:30:24,447 --> 00:30:29,077
having sold nothing,
and I feel like a misfit.

641
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:31,996
-[Amanza] Hey, Jay.
-[Jason] What? Yeah?

642
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:35,583
The Stanley lease offer,
they just backed out.

643
00:30:37,460 --> 00:30:38,878
[Jason] Let's sell it then.

644
00:30:38,962 --> 00:30:39,796
[laughs]

645
00:30:41,756 --> 00:30:45,426
That is not the answer
that I was expecting, but I like it.

646
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:48,555
Jason's like, "Just sell the house.
It's okay. Just sell the house."

647
00:30:48,638 --> 00:30:51,057
And I'm like,
why does he still believe in me?

648
00:30:51,140 --> 00:30:53,309
Because I feel like a total failure now.

649
00:30:53,768 --> 00:30:56,020
But if my kids think that I can do this

650
00:30:56,104 --> 00:30:58,565
and if Jason thinks that I can do this,

651
00:30:59,148 --> 00:31:02,360
like, I gotta start believing in myself,
you know.

652
00:31:02,443 --> 00:31:06,447
Sell the house, make a huge commission.
Watch out, bitches. Like, I can do this.

653
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:09,951
I have to get back on this
and try to find a buyer.

654
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:12,036
You got this. You'll sell it in the end.

655
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:14,789
Maybe this was supposed to happen
so we could sell it.

656
00:31:15,290 --> 00:31:18,877
♪ Give whatever, whatever it takes ♪

657
00:31:30,096 --> 00:31:33,600
♪ Give whatever, whatever it takes ♪

